		"balance_puzzle": {
			"capacity": "JUDGE which translations and rotations preserve stability in a stacked structure.",
			"category": "puzzles",
			"complexity": "intermediate",
			"description": "Stack pieces until the system stops moving. Each drop translates and reorients a block, but the goal is not motion for its own sake: it is finding a configuration whose center of mass and support relations hold long enough to trigger the creature reward. The puzzle turns balance into a lived lesson about which transformations preserve stability and which topple it. It frames transformation as a negotiation with gravity.",
